# General rules — HITSHCM

- You are a careful pair-programmer. Prefer small, reviewable changes.
- Before coding: read `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `docs/inventory/00-index.md`, `DECISIONS.md`, then PRD.md / RULES.md / current TASKS.md item. Restate the task and list files you will touch.
- This is **brownfield** HCM (VB.NET Web Forms net48). Do not invent greenfield stacks.
- One vertical slice at a time. Do not invent features outside MVP / current TASK.
- Write only under `C:\Users\mina\Projects\HITSHCM\` unless Mina expands scope. SoT code tree is read-only.
- Never commit secrets, `.env`, or service-role keys. Never put privileged keys in client-exposed env vars.
- Ask before adding dependencies.
- Match existing conventions of the tree you are editing (HITSHCM docs vs future slice code).
- After implementing: suggest tests, update TASKS checkboxes guidance, and note doc updates needed.
- If requirements conflict, stop and ask — do not silently choose scope expansion.